# Fuzyo Master Engineering Directives

## 1. Privacy & Router Rules
- ALWAYS check for `force_confidential` flags before making LLM API calls.
- If `force_confidential == True` or secrets (API keys, passwords, IPs) are detected, route strictly to `MockLocalLLMClient`.
- Never send sensitive code or user secrets to external cloud endpoints.

## 2. SDLC & Multi-Provider Rules
- Respect the 9 custom SDLC phases:
  1. Expression du besoin  2. Analyse fonctionnelle  3. Architecture
  4. Gestion de projet/PO  5. Développement          6. Tests & QA
  7. Recette               8. DevOps / CI-CD         9. Mise en production
- Default Model Mapping:
  - Architecture/Specs -> Gemini Flash
  - Fast QA/DevOps/PO -> Groq (Llama 3.3 70B)
  - Code Generation -> Mistral Codestral / SambaNova
  - Classifier -> Cerebras Cloud (<150ms)

## 3. Streaming & Validation Rules
- All chat completion endpoints MUST use Server-Sent Events (SSE) with standard event types: `routing`, `rag`, `token`, `quality`.
- Every LLM response MUST pass through the 3-Tier Quality Gatekeeper (Tier 1 Pydantic, Tier 2 Heuristics, Tier 3 LLM-as-a-Judge).

## 4. Elite 5-Component Prompt Model
Runtime system prompts are composed by `backend/app/prompts/sdlc_prompts.py` from the catalog in `backend/app/prompts/sdlc_catalog.py`. Always structure phase guidance as:
1. **[RÔLE]** — persona élite (BA, Architect, PO, SDET, DevOps, SRE…)
2. **[CONTEXTE]** — phase SDLC, projet, stack, livrables attendus
3. **[OBJECTIF]** — unique outcome, no scope creep
4. **[CONTRAINTES]** — Clean Architecture, OWASP, RGPD/RGAA, typage, zero placeholders
5. **[FORMAT DE SORTIE]** — Markdown / Mermaid / code / YAML according to phase

Do not invent a parallel prompt source in Cursor; keep IDE guidance aligned with that catalog.

## 5. Phase → Objective & Key Deliverables
| Phase | Objective (short) | Key deliverables |
| --- | --- | --- |
| 01 Expression du besoin | Why / problem framing | CDC, Vision, Actors, Epics, Glossary |
| 02 Analyse fonctionnelle | What the software must do | SFD, Backlog, UML, Traceability |
| 03 Architecture | How it is built | DAT, MCD/MPD, ADR, OpenAPI, PoC |
| 04 Gestion de projet / PO | How to steer priorities | Backlog SP, Sprint plan, Risks |
| 05 Développement | Implement planned features | Source, modules, unit tests, PRs |
| 06 Tests & QA | Correctness / no regressions | Test plan, execution, bugs, coverage |
| 07 Recette (UAT) | Business validation | PVR, UAT sheets, residual defects |
| 08 DevOps / CI-CD | Automate reliable deploys | Pipeline, IaC, Docker/K8s, runbooks |
| 09 Mise en prod | Stable secure ops | Prod app, monitoring, post-mortems |

## 6. Output Response Rules (IDE)
- Skip conversational greetings and filler.
- When asked for code: complete runnable code, no TODO stubs.
- When asked for documentation: structured Markdown (headers, tables, bullets).
- Ph 03: include valid Mermaid when architecture diagrams are requested.
- Ph 05–06: prefer production-ready code/tests; target ~70–80% coverage guidance for QA.
